{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages","id":945024,"title":"[2E] Prometheans and Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-06T13:18:50-07:00","id":945024,"title":"[2E] Prometheans and Mages","content":"As we had premier of <b>Promethean: The Created</b> 2E, I want to add some Created character ( maybe PC, maybe NPC ) to our Alchemy based <b>Mage</b> game ( about one you can read <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/825300-cod-mage-magnum-opus-actual-play\">more here</a> ). As we do not have proper 2E crossover rules ( <u>yet</u> - because there comes <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle\">whole book about crossovers</a>! ) some homebrews will be in order. Posted on Mage forum as they are definitely more complex part of crossover equation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So let\u2019s help our mages uncover secrets of Divine Fire and Alchemy!<br /> <br /> Here are some opening questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>What will see Awakened when looking with Mage Sight on Promethean?</b> Clearly Peripheral MS will do *ping*, but what about Active and Focus? ( Yes, best would be answer based on Arcana. )</li> <li><b>What Arcana can work on Promethean?</b> Is it Life as with living being? Is it Matter as of inorganic body and Humors it\u2019s made off? What about Constructs ( non-human bodies Created ) or Unfleashed ( \u2018robots\u2019 and automatons ) \u2013 are they \u2018living\u2019 for Supernal Magic? Or inorganic and under Matter?</li> <li><b>How could mages can control or collect Pyros?</b> I think that Prime should be enough, like vampires abilities are controlled by Death and werewolves are by Spirit \u2013 but I\u2019m not sure about it.</li> <li><b>How can Awakened become or make someone resistant to Disquiet Conditions?</b> I suspect Mind 2 will be enough as it sounds like Ruling or Shielding effect of Mind Arcanum \u2013 still cannot decide which.</li> <li><b>Can mages see past Azoth illusion? </b>Or will the see everything like Sleepers see Promethean? Can they sense Azothic Radiance?</li> <li><b>Can Awakened somehow perceive internal Alchemy of Refinement inside Created? </b>Like seeing that two Prometheans from same Linage are on different Refinements and knowing they are different beside look?</li> <li><b>Can mages sense or stop Wasteland created by Promethean?</b> If yes, what Arcana and it\u2019s level will it need?</li> <li><b>Can Perfected Metals be somehow linked or resonant with Refinements? </b>Can mages sense connection to Metals of those ( like Aurum being Gold or Aes being Bronze )?</li> <li><b>What \u2018nice\u2019 effects can Firestorm have on Awakened?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ol>Will wrote more questions if get more of them in my sick mind\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T13:54:18-07:00","id":945045,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that in the Book of the Dead, Prometheans had to roll to determine if the Underworld treats them as alive or dead. So whatever else, we know that Death is likely useful for identifying the Created with Mage Sigh, though it would probably give you really confusing symbols to interpret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:39:06-07:00","id":945071,"title":"","content":"To answer #9, certain kinds of Firestorms can eliminate a Wasteland, restoring the area to its normal state.<br /> <br /> (Just going to tackle these in no particular order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T19:30:49-07:00","id":945231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What will see Awakened when looking with Mage Sight on Promethean?</b> Clearly Peripheral MS will do *ping*, but what about Active and Focus? ( Yes, best would be answer based on Arcana. )<br /> <b>What Arcana can work on Promethean?</b> Is it Life as with living being? Is it Matter as of inorganic body and Humors it\u2019s made off? What about Constructs ( non-human bodies Created ) or Unfleashed ( \u2018robots\u2019 and automatons ) \u2013 are they \u2018living\u2019 for Supernal Magic? Or inorganic and under Matter?<br /> <b>How could mages can control or collect Pyros?</b> I think that Prime should be enough, like vampires abilities are controlled by Death and werewolves are by Spirit \u2013 but I\u2019m not sure about it.<br /> <b>How can Awakened become or make someone resistant to Disquiet Conditions?</b> I suspect Mind 2 will be enough as it sounds like Ruling or Shielding effect of Mind Arcanum \u2013 still cannot decide which.<br /> <b>Can mages see past Azoth illusion? </b>Or will the see everything like Sleepers see Promethean? Can they sense Azothic Radiance?<br /> <b>Can Awakened somehow perceive internal Alchemy of Refinement inside Created? </b>Like seeing that two Prometheans from same Linage are on different Refinements and knowing they are different beside look?<br /> <b>Can mages sense or stop Wasteland created by Promethean?</b> If yes, what Arcana and it\u2019s level will it need?<br /> <b>Can Perfected Metals be somehow linked or resonant with Refinements? </b>Can mages sense connection to Metals of those ( like Aurum being Gold or Aes being Bronze )?<br /> <b>What \u2018nice\u2019 effects can Firestorm have on Awakened?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In order:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Well, the thing is that the Fire doesn't play nice with the Supernal. Prime Sight will ping that something is happening, but it won't make sense. Life and Death will both ping, and it also won't make sense. Fate <i>might</i> ping if you buy into the idea that the Fire has a plan for the Created and thus a destiny, and Matter might also ping considering the crazy alchemical shit going on in there. Redeemed Prometheans might ping for Time and Space since the Dawn seems to retroactively edit the Prommy's past, unless I misread that section.</li> <li>Depends what you want. If you're trying to do something to its body as an animate being, it'd be Life, but if you're actually working with its structure, it'd be Matter. I think an Unfleshed would count as &quot;living&quot; for Supernal magic, but with the rider that it's not quite there, like a normal Promethean.</li> <li>I think Strange Alchemies had Qashmallim as being affected by Prime/Mind, and since divinity and magic are under Prime's purview, Pyros would probably be manipulated by Prime. It might be exotic enough that you'd need Reach to play with it.</li> <li>It can be either. I'd go with Shielding (protecting the Mind from its effects), but Ruling might be applicable (Forcing your mind to ignore the Disquiet).</li> <li>Well, they might ping on Peripheral sight, but I think they might have to actually used Focused sight to penetrate the illusion.</li> <li>Again, that'd probably be something to ping on Peripheral sight. Unless they can see through things, though, they'll need magic to actually see it happening.</li> <li>Well, that's tough. They could probably suppress a Wasteland's effect with various Arcana, using Ruling. You might prevent it from taking hold with Prime Shielding. You might try to clean it up with Prime Fraying or Perfecting depending on exactly how you do it.</li> <li>I love this idea so much. Maybe Perfected Metal charms can be used to help appropriate Transmutations? Or maybe they just make good Athanors for Transmutations for that Refinement?</li> <li>For starters, I like the idea of the Fire screwing with Supernal magic. Some of the Mage's Mana gets &quot;ignited&quot; into Pyros and behaves wildly when it's expended, triggering something that's like Paradox but not Abyssal.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:12:18-07:00","id":945969,"title":"","content":"All of these answers are, obviously, just how I would run it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>What will see Awakened when looking with Mage Sight on Promethean?</b> Clearly Peripheral MS will do *ping*, but what about Active and Focus? ( Yes, best would be answer based on Arcana. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime AMS would register them, and show them something similar to occasional bursts of something similar to Celestial Fire within the Promethean.<br /> Matter AMS would register them as being entirely composed to it, as opposed to Life or Death<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>What Arcana can work on Promethean?</b> Is it Life as with living being? Is it Matter as of inorganic body and Humors it\u2019s made off? What about Constructs ( non-human bodies Created ) or Unfleashed ( \u2018robots\u2019 and automatons ) \u2013 are they \u2018living\u2019 for Supernal Magic? Or inorganic and under Matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>All Prometheans are constructs, even if they aren't all 'constructs'. I'd have their physical bodies be affected exclusively by Matter. Powers would be affected by Prime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>How could mages can control or collect Pyros?</b> I think that Prime should be enough, like vampires abilities are controlled by Death and werewolves are by Spirit \u2013 but I\u2019m not sure about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime, if you allow it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>How can Awakened become or make someone resistant to Disquiet Conditions?</b> I suspect Mind 2 will be enough as it sounds like Ruling or Shielding effect of Mind Arcanum \u2013 still cannot decide which.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime shielding for shielding against the effects, or a Mind spell that counteracts the effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Can mages see past Azoth illusion? </b>Or will the see everything like Sleepers see Promethean? Can they sense Azothic Radiance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't let them see pass the illusion or sense Azothic Radiance by default, but both would be doable by Prime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Can Awakened somehow perceive internal Alchemy of Refinement inside Created? </b>Like seeing that two Prometheans from same Linage are on different Refinements and knowing they are different beside look?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow that kind of perception with Prime or Matter Focused Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Can mages sense or stop Wasteland created by Promethean?</b> If yes, what Arcana and it\u2019s level will it need?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime Unveiling to sense it, Fraying or potentially Unmaking to remove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Can Perfected Metals be somehow linked or resonant with Refinements? </b>Can mages sense connection to Metals of those ( like Aurum being Gold or Aes being Bronze )?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want them to be<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages#post945024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>What \u2018nice\u2019 effects can Firestorm have on Awakened?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>More on this later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 08-08-2016, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T12:52:55-07:00","id":961181,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking on some little twist to Disquite rules for mages - I think that more interesting image than 'torches and pitchforks', is Mysterium mages wanting to dissect living Promethean. So maybe Disquieted mages changes one of their Obsessions to the Promethean itself? But on what stadium would it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:48:36-07:00","id":961217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=961181#post961181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So maybe Disquieted mages changes one of their Obsessions to the Promethean itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a realy neat idea.<br /> <br /> [/quote]But on what stadium would it be?[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I don't understand what you're saying there. Do you mean, what exactly would trigger the change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:04:45-07:00","id":961225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=961217#post961217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what you're saying there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stage. He's asking what stage of Disquiet the proposed effect should kick in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:20:48-07:00","id":961233,"title":"","content":"Hm. Does it sound plausible that Prime Shielding can make an area resistant to Wastelands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T20:04:33-07:00","id":961371,"title":"","content":"OK; I'm seeing nothing in the Actual Play thread to indicate that you're deviating from the standard assumptions about mages and Prometheans, so I'll be responding accordingly.<br /> <br /> 1. I would not assume that Peripheral Mage Sight <i>would</i> ping on Pyros, as Pyros doesn't have any associated symbols to ping off of. Likewise, Active Mage Sight likely wouldn't pick up anything concerning Pyros, and Scrutinizing Pyros would pick up Nothing -- not even the usual ambient supernal signatures, just a void. OTOH, an Unveiling <i>spell</i>, cast by a mage who has already become somewhat familiar with the Divine Fire, would be able to pick up the presence of Pyros. Call it Prime/Fate or Death/Fate, depending on whether you're dealing with Elpis-oriented manifestations of Pyros or Flux-oriented manifestations. <br /> 2. On the Promethean itself? Either Life or Matter, depending on whether it's made of flesh or not. So Unfleshed and Constructs would be Matter; everyone else would be Life. <br /> 3. Mages cannot control or collect Pyros. Not using Supernal Magic, at least. If they forego Magic, they can attempt to collect or control Pyros the same way <b>Promethean</b>'s Alchemists do; but that tends to have harmful effects on their Gnosis. See <b>Saturnine Night</b> concerning mages who try to create Prometheans. The exception to this is a spell in <b>Strange Alchemies</b> that allows Supernal Magic to harm <i>qashmallim</i>; but there's no indication that that goes beyond Fraying; it may not even go to Unraveling or Unmaking. In particular, I'd say that Compelling, Ruling, Perfecting, Weaving, Patterning, and Making are entirely off-limits where Pyros is concerned. You can sense and study it, protect against it, and harm it; that's all. And I'd say that even those effects arguably involve indirect approaches and caution, like handling hot metal using tongs. <br /> 4. Disquiet can be protected against using Mind Shielding. Per Dave, this isn't about manipulating Pyros; it's about shielding one's own mind. <br /> 5. Disfigurements can be revealed by an Unveiling spell, assuming the mage has prior experience with Prometheans. Azothic Radiance likewise can be detected by an Unveiling spell or examined by a Knowing spell -- again, if the mage knows to look for them. <br /> 6. A Knowing spell could reveal details about a Promethean's Lineage and Refinement. <br /> 7. I could see Shielding an area against the Wasteland Effect, in the same way that one can Shield one's mind against Disquiet. It's not the Pyros that your spell is affecting; it's the land. <br /> 8. The metals are allegories, not literal associations; so no, there aren't associations between the Perfected Metals and the Refinements. <br /> 9. Firestorms generally don't have nice effects for anyone; but when they do, they tend to benefit mages the same way they benefit anyone else. <br /> <br /> The Divine Fire features its own kind of Alchemy, just as the Supernal World does; but they are <i>not</i> compatible with each other, despite superficial appearances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T22:10:36-07:00","id":961449,"title":"","content":"I went with the interpretation of Pyros as the force of Change itself, with additional symbolism of divine revelation and spiritual energy. As change is listed as one of the purviews of Time, I'm going to rule that equal amounts of Time + Prime are needed for spells related to Pyros - with the caveat that many here also use, that supernal magic can't directly affect it, but can study, shield against it, and nudge it indirectly.<br /> <br /> To emphasize it's role as being unpredictable change, I'm also ruling that any magic that targets Pyros or something using it is warped, gaining 1 Reach effect as per an Anomaly Paradox per point of Pyros in the target (ie, a power that costs 2 Pyros to use inflicts two Reach on magic to unwravvel it, but, say, a Knowing spell that targets a Quashmallim suffers its full Pyros pool in extra Reach).<br /> <br /> Just my two cents. I'm also tinkering with rules for various crossover, as I just started running a Mage game and want to use these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T21:42:53-07:00","id":963092,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to wonder if mages should be able to manipulate Divine Fire at all. This post sums up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle?p=963071#post963071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A promethean book had rules for mages being able to sense pyros, and that was explicitly all they could do- sense it, no creating it, destroying it, or affecting it in anyway.<br /> <br /> Even in the mage book about archmasters who could create werewolves with vampire disciplines and changeling contracts, prometheans and transmutations are noticeable by their absence.<br /> <br /> Now of course in second edition they can change whatever they want, but in 1st edition it was pretty clear that as awesome as controlling the 10 arcana are, Pyros was classified as none of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if Pyros at large can be Prime spell, should he be able to be molded by mages in to it's variants, like Elpis with Prime-Fate and Flux with Prime-Death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-04-2016, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:57:53-07:00","id":963317,"title":"","content":"The first question should be how well do you want Mages and Prometheans to work together. If you want a Promethean to join their cabal (or Mage a Throng) then you will have to provide a way to deal with Disquiet and Wasteland effects.<br /> \u200bAs for pinging Peripheral Sight, only if the Promethean does something that requires him to spend Pyros, his existence alone shouldn't.<br /> For Focused Sight I would give the Promethean an Opacity rating, then wish hostile Mages good luck at getting a Promethean to sit still long enough for them to study him.<br /> In my opinion Perfected Metals should provide a benefit towards Refinements, symbolically a Perfected Metal is the metal in its own most refined state.<br /> I could see Mages containing Pyros but controlling it in a usable fashion should at the least be the subject of a long term Obsession, not easy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:54:23-07:00","id":963343,"title":"","content":"One thought I've had for Mage/Created interactions is that, in addition to whatever else they read as, Matter Sight sees them as being made out of whatever metal their current Refinement is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T21:31:50-07:00","id":963531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=963317#post963317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first question should be how well do you want Mages and Prometheans to work together. If you want a Promethean to join their cabal (or Mage a Throng) then you will have to provide a way to deal with Disquiet and Wasteland effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Created joining the cabal crossover variant. <b>Solution for Disquiet is simple</b> - Mind Shielding Practice, so Mind 2 is all needed, one PC have this.<br /> <br /> Wasteland is more tricky as ( for now ) mages do not know anything solid about Promethean condition. I think that Shielding Practice of Prime over area should do the trick, but then we make precedent over controlling the Divine Fire with Supernal Magic and this can lead to bad stuff, away from <b>CoD</b> canon...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=963317#post963317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAs for pinging Peripheral Sight, only if the Promethean does something that requires him to spend Pyros, his existence alone shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sound fair here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=963317#post963317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bFor Focused Sight I would give the Promethean an Opacity rating, then wish hostile Mages good luck at getting a Promethean to sit still long enough for them to study him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Opacity from <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9YzBRVWpGYzNFZ0U/view\" target=\"_blank\">spoiled rules from <b>Signs of Sorcery</b></a>? Basic Opacity would be then like Azoth of character, if I'm not mistaken?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=963317#post963317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIn my opinion Perfected Metals should provide a benefit towards Refinements, symbolically a Perfected Metal is the metal in its own most refined state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have anything on the mind?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=963317#post963317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI could see Mages containing Pyros but controlling it in a usable fashion should at the least be the subject of a long term Obsession, not easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, controling Divine Fire will be second big Mystery to be Obsessed for in chronicle ( first is Supernal Alchemy ). With Created himself as probably third one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T06:52:54-07:00","id":963671,"title":"","content":"If you have someone skilled in Space there is one simple solution for wasteland. Have a pocket realm where the promethean spends most of their time, count it as &quot;being elsewhere&quot; for the purposes of the wasteland effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:31:09-07:00","id":963775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=963671#post963671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have someone skilled in Space there is one simple solution for wasteland. Have a pocket realm where the promethean spends most of their time, count it as &quot;being elsewhere&quot; for the purposes of the wasteland effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, y'know, persistent shortcut to their Hovel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T10:42:01-07:00","id":963782,"title":"","content":"Took the words right outta my mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:23:23-07:00","id":964232,"title":"","content":"Thinking more about my idea for Disquite on mages - <b>I wonder what Stage choose to make Obsession change on Awakened?</b> Stage Three sounds as total obsession that leads slowly to 'pitchforks and torches' for Sleepers, but I think it's too late for mages. They're drive for uncovering Mysteries should kick earlier. Question is simple - Stage One or Stage Two?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, page 308</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Stage Two on Sleepers sounds as totally driving off the Created from mages, so some change could be in order.The victim refuses to have anything to do with the Promethean. Any attempt to force the matter will result in the victim becoming violent.<br /> \u2022 If the victim and the Promethean are in the same place, he will do everything in his power to drive the Promethean from the premises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically original Stage Two would mages <i>avoid</i> Promethean, not Obsessed over him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On the other hand, original Stage One is <i>very</i> easily to get ( in game play terms ). Each mage should automatically get this from just using Mage Sight on Promethean first time.<br /> <br /> <b>So maybe good middle point would be changing Stage Two for mages that they must take Created as one of their Obsessions?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T23:31:33-07:00","id":969041,"title":"","content":"Few more topics that spring to my mind when reading new PtC corebook...<br /> <br /> 1. In book is this passage:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, page 169</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once per day, a Promethean regains a point of Pyros if she spends an hour or more around humans.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Does this mean Created get\u2019s 1 Pyros from interactions with with mages, as Awakened are humans?</b><br /> <br /> 2. Does this also leads to Disquiet? Rules says those are factors to generating it in victim:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, page 173</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>A mortal spends a full scene in superficial social contact with the Promethean. Additional scenes in the same chapter do not count as another trigger.</li> <li>A Promethean attempts to seduce, persuade, intimidate, or otherwise manipulate the mortal, whether through using Skill rolls or Social maneuvering (see p. 202).</li> <li>A character uses supernatural senses on a Promethean, such as the Unseen Sense Merit or the various detection and scrutiny-related powers of supernatural beings.</li> <li>A mortal witnesses a Promethean\u2019s disfigurements (see p. 171).</li> <li>The mortal and the Promethean engage in a conversation lasting more than a few minutes, or exchange personal information (even falsified).</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><b>So can mage generate Pyros in Created by interacting with them, but risk Disquiet?</b><br /> <br /> <b>3. Does alchemical formulas works as High Speech? </b>Can they be \u2018decoded\u2019 by mages, uncovering Supernal Symbols connected to them? In game we will have Created in whole tattooed in those after his demiurges wanting to transplant his mind to new body and making Promethean instead\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T02:38:10-07:00","id":977671,"title":"","content":"Tinkering a bit, I think about this spread of connected Conditions to Disquiet in mages would look like this:<br /> 1. Disquieted - Stage 1, Change of one of mages Obsessions to Promethean and it's locked, until character has Disquieted Condition.<br /> 2. Disquieted - Stage 2, Obsession Condition for mage on Promethean.<br /> 3. Disquieted - Stage 3<br /> 4. Disquieted - Stage 4<br /> <br /> So here are question on this idea:<br /> 1. Can mages shed Disquieted Condition by Mind magic ones he get it? Maybe Mind 3 <i>Clear Thoughts</i> with Reach?<br /> 2. If mage can shed Disquiet - Will this automatically take off connected Obsession on Promethean? Or does Obsession is totally different than Mind Arcanum preview?<br /> <br /> <b>lnodiv</b>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar451_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"451\" data-vbnamecard=\"451\">Kirby Jerusalem</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I would like your thoughts on this, if I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-28-2016, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T04:58:10-07:00","id":977690,"title":"","content":"In 1e, shedding Disquiet involved a spell for altering memories: you literally have to forget about the incident that generated the Disquiet in order to be free of it.<br /> <br /> Also, I wouldn't change a mage's Obsessions any sooner than Stage 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T05:52:48-07:00","id":977709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/945024-2e-prometheans-and-mages?p=977690#post977690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I wouldn't change a mage's Obsessions any sooner than Stage 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stage 3 comes now only in Wasteland area. As Wasteland is rather <i>rare</i> - and it's effects are more than obvious to mages, then Awakened would not get any time Obsession shift.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Disquiet roll is Promie's Azoth vs Resolve + Composure of mage - as Awakened have typically higher those pools than normal, getting any Disquieted Stage is <i>rare</i> event for mages. I'm okay in those unfortunate making instant Obsession on Created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}